import{_ as t,o as a,c as i,a5 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CsGesDJn.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Acceptance checks","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"feature/ltx-director-worker/test.md","filePath":"feature/ltx-director-worker/test.md"}'),r={name:"feature/ltx-director-worker/test.md"};function s(n,e,c,d,l,u){return a(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="acceptance-checks" tabindex="-1">Acceptance checks <a class="header-anchor" href="#acceptance-checks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Acceptance checks&quot;">​</a></h1><ul><li>Importing builder performs no filesystem write or CLI action. Both example scripts build outside the source checkout.</li><li>Review requires character; cinematic rejects an unexpected character. Keyframe IDs are unique K0–K3; exactly two parts; bounded voice timings.</li><li>Expanded graph contains no UUID class types or editor-only nodes. Parent image links, promoted text/seed values, K1 end guide and Part-1-last-frame→Part-2 continuity are retained.</li><li>Unsupported widget serialization, missing runtime nodes and unresolved required inputs fail before GPU submission.</li><li>Missing/wrong API key is rejected before multipart parsing; oversize image/body is rejected.</li><li>Mock ComfyUI receives uniquely named uploads and a valid API graph, returns job id; polling exposes only output media, failures and pending state correctly.</li><li>Backend chooses LTX only for configured 20-second image jobs, with character→review and no character→cinematic. Existing Animate/I2V regressions pass.</li><li>Business preserves legacy constructors and forwards the optional character image without changing credit/idempotency behavior.</li><li>UI character upload accepts supported images, can remove them, and sends the selected image. Labels exist in vi/en and reuse theme tokens.</li><li>ZIP contains a portable worker/builder/director and excludes all secrets. Do not count mock success as a GPU quality pass.</li></ul><h2 id="results-—-2026-11-10" tabindex="-1">Results — 2026-11-10 <a class="header-anchor" href="#results-—-2026-11-10" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Results — 2026-11-10&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Portable builder/converter/worker: <code>python -m unittest discover -s tests -v</code>: 8 passed. Covers both canvases, continuity, promoted values, seed UI controls, bypassed LoRA, unsupported node rejection, auth/mode validation and mocked submission.</li><li>AI backend: <code>pytest tests/unit/services/test_ltx_worker.py tests/unit/services/test_i2v_worker.py -q</code>: 12 passed, with mocked Claude and worker HTTP; no paid call or render.</li><li>Business: focused <code>AiVideoCharacterTest</code>: 2 passed, 0 failures/errors, preserving legacy constructors and forwarding optional character.</li><li>Web: <code>npm run ci</code> passed (110 existing lint warnings, 0 errors); <code>npx tsc -b</code> passed after the final 20-second job polling timeout adjustment.</li><li>ZIP: 32 explicitly allowed files, 4,498,884 bytes. CRC check passed; extracted into an isolated temporary directory and built review/cinematic canvases plus imported API/OpenAPI without the original checkout or sibling Ovi repo. No keys, <code>.env</code>, logs, model weights or caches included.</li><li>Read-only final review found no concrete blocker; it explicitly did not certify actual installed ComfyUI schema compatibility.</li></ul><p>Still pending: actual <code>/object_info</code> conversion for both full templates on the VM, GPU memory/quality and Vietnamese voice checks, live polling/media/S3 delivery, browser light/dark checks and public worker configuration. VM is off at the user&#39;s request. <code>start_api.py</code> performs schema compilation before exposing a new worker; failure requires diagnosis before claiming deployment success.</p><p>Deployment: upload the ZIP, extract under <code>/workspace</code>, run <code>bash /workspace/ltx_video_bundle/setup.sh</code>. Public API targets 10200, GUI targets 10101. Backend LTX URL/key settings remain opt-in; a built ZIP is not evidence that the web is connected to a live worker. Stable <code>API_KEY</code> in the VM <code>.env</code> can be reused across rentals; an automatically generated key changes on a fresh VM and must be updated privately in backend settings.</p><h2 id="revision-2026-11-18-vace" tabindex="-1">Revision 2026-11-18 (VACE) <a class="header-anchor" href="#revision-2026-11-18-vace" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Revision 2026-11-18 (VACE)&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Worker: missing key 401 on /health and submit; bad script and GIF upload 422; media path traversal 400; real unbox_perfume canvas compiles (subgraph expanded, LoadImage = uploaded name only, one SaveVideo <code>video/vace_&lt;job&gt;</code>); completed job lists the MP4.</li><li>Director: both examples validate and reach the worker with <code>script_json</code>; character adds an <code>extra_images</code> part; size follows aspect ratio; segment 1 <code>prev</code>, out-of-range panel, non-4n+1 frames and a 30 s script are rejected without a submit.</li><li>Live (pending): <code>/health</code> through ngrok returned ok with key, 401 without (2026-11-18). GPU render not yet run.</li><li>Web (product-video): submit disabled without product photo or brief; brief capped at 1000; GIF/oversize rejected with a message; generate sends duration 20 + images; completed job shows the video; failure shows the error. Check both themes.</li></ul>',8)])])}const m=t(r,[["render",s]]);export{h as __pageData,m as default};
